## Run order (development)

<%
const runHints = {
  'quarkus-rest': './gradlew quarkusDev',
  'go-http': 'go run ./cmd/http',
  'rust-http': 'cargo run',
  'web-components': 'npm run dev',
};
const backendService = services[0];
const frontendService = services[services.length - 1];
-%>
1. Start the backend first:
   ```sh
   cd <%= backendService.path %> && <%= runHints[backendService.stack] ?? 'see its README' %>   # serves http://localhost:8080
   ```
2. Then the frontend dev server:
   ```sh
   cd <%= frontendService.path %> && <%= runHints[frontendService.stack] ?? 'see its README' %>   # proxies /api → localhost:8080
   ```

The frontend reaches the backend through its `gateway-rest` driven
port; in development Vite proxies `/api`, in production set
`VITE_API_BASE_URL` at build time (12-factor: config via env). The
wire itself is pinned by the backend's
[`contract/greet.openapi.yaml`](<%= backendService.path %>/contract/greet.openapi.yaml).

## Run containerised

```sh
docker compose up --build   # SPA on http://localhost:8081, /api proxied to the backend
```

One image per deployment unit, built from the Dockerfile beside it.

## Working here

Each service is independently buildable and testable — see its own
README. Changes that cross services (e.g. the greet contract) land as
one commit in this repository.
